 ### Bilinear Image Sampling
-Samples colors from a batch of images at specified 2D pixel coordinates. Takes `images` tensor of shape `[batch_size, H, W, C]` and `xy_grid` of shape `[N, 2]`. Flips `xy_grid` sign, reshapes to `[batch_size, N, 1, 2]`. Permutes images to `[batch_size, C, H, W]`. Uses `torch.nn.functional.grid_sample` with `align_corners=True` and `mode="bilinear"` [S15, unofficial]. `align_corners=True` ensures corner pixels align with grid boundaries during interpolation, preventing coordinate scaling artifacts at image edges [S15, unofficial].
+Samples colors from a batch of images at specified 2D pixel coordinates. Takes `images` tensor of shape `[batch_size, H, W, C]` and `xy_grid` of shape `[N, 2]`. Flips `xy_grid` sign, reshapes to `[batch_size, N, 1, 2]`. Permutes images to `[batch_size, C, H, W]`. Uses `torch.nn.functional.grid_sample` with `align_corners=True` and `mode="bilinear"` [S16, unofficial]. The parameter `align_corners=True` ensures corner pixels align with grid boundaries during interpolation, preventing coordinate scaling artifacts at image edges [S16, unofficial].
 
 ### Labelmap Transfer Function LUT Construction
-Constructs two 1D LUT textures (soft and hard) for labelmap transfer functions. The soft LUT uses float precision and bilinear filtering; the hard LUT uses byte precision and point filtering [S4, unofficial]. Initializes floatPixels array of size 256 with Color(0,0,0,0) and bytePixels array of size 256 with Color32(0,0,0,0) [S4, unofficial]. If data.tf.entries is not null, iterates over each entry e, calculates idx as Mathf.Clamp(Mathf.RoundToInt(e.label), 0, lutSize-1), extracts r, g, b from e.color (default 0f) and a from e.alpha, stores in floatPixels[idx] [S4, unofficial]. Converts r, g, b, a from float [0,1] to byte [0,255] by multiplying by 255, rounding, and clamping to [0,255], stores in bytePixels [S4, unofficial]. Creates lutSoft as Texture2D(lutSize, 1, RGBAFloat, false) with wrapMode Clamp, filterMode Bilinear, sets pixels from floatPixels and applies [S4, unofficial]. Creates lutHard as Texture2D(lutSize, 1, RGBA32, false) with wrapMode Clamp, filterMode Point, sets pixels32 from bytePixels and applies [S4, unofficial]. Assigns lutSoft to data.tfLUTTextureSoft and lutHard to data.tfLUTTextureHard [S4, unofficial]. lutSize is a constant integer value 256, representing the maximum number of labels [S4, unofficial].
+Constructs two 1D LUT textures (soft and hard) for labelmap transfer functions. The soft LUT uses float precision and bilinear filtering; the hard LUT uses byte precision and point filtering [S4, unofficial]. It initializes float and byte pixel arrays of size 256, maps label indices to colors, converts float RGBA to byte, and uploads them as `Texture2D` with appropriate wrap/filter modes (`Clamp`/`Bilinear` for soft, `Clamp`/`Point` for hard) [S4, unofficial].
 
 ### 2D Transfer Function
-A volume rendering technique that maps two separate scalar fields to color and opacity using a 2D lookup table (image), extending the 1D transfer function approach [S16]. The X-axis represents the scalar `value` and the Y-axis represents the gradient of the value, grad(value) [S16]. Unlike separable 1D transfer functions which combine two 1D lookups (potentially saving memory), the 2D TFN allows for non-separable, arbitrary 2D mappings without implementation constraints on combination [S16].
+A volume rendering technique that maps two separate scalar fields to color and opacity using a 2D lookup table (image), extending the 1D transfer function approach [S17]. It uses a `lookupTable` which is an `ARRAY2D` of Color objects, where width and height represent two separate scalar fields. A pitfall is the ambiguity in mapping scalar fields to the 2D lookup table axes; a prescriptive interpretation is that the X-axis represents the scalar `value` and the Y-axis represents the gradient of the value, `grad(value)` [S17]. Unlike separable 1D transfer functions, the 2D TFN allows for non-separable, arbitrary 2D mappings [S17].
 
 ### Material Synchronization LUT Adjustment
-An algorithm to adjust a 1D Look-Up Table (LUT) mapping sample values to material indices, ensuring that the distribution of sample values across materials is synchronized with the frame number and material centers [S17, unofficial]. Calculates the common base allocation range `d` as `frameNumber / colorKind`. Initializes material center positions `indexM[i]` to `d*i + d / 2` for each material `i` from 0 to `colorKind - 1` [S17, unofficial]. Decrements the count for the selected material `minIndex` and stores `minIndex` in `temp[i]` [S17, unofficial].
+An algorithm to adjust a 1D Look-Up Table (LUT) mapping sample values to material indices, ensuring that the distribution of sample values across materials is synchronized with the frame number and material centers [S18, unofficial]. It calculates a common base allocation range `d` as `frameNumber / colorKind` and initializes material center positions `indexM[i]` to `d*i + d / 2` [S18, unofficial].
 
 ### BuildFunctionFromTable
-Constructs a color transfer function from a pre-existing table of colors [S18]. After calling this method, the function range will be [x1, x2] [S18]. The function will have size nodes [S18]. Function values will be regularly spaced between x1 and x2 [S18]. The table parameter's layout is assumed to be [R1, G1, B1, R2, G2, B2, ..., Rn, Gn, Bn], and it is assumed to be a block of memory of size [3*size] [S18].
+Constructs a color transfer function from a pre-existing table of colors [S19]. The function range will be $[x_1, x_2]$, the function will have size `nodes`, and function values will be regularly spaced between $x_1$ and $x_2$ [S19]. The table parameter's layout is assumed to be $[R_1, G_1, B_1, R_2, G_2, B_2, \dots, R_n, G_n, B_n]$, a block of memory of size $[3 \times size]$ [S19].
 
